\section*{Unbounded positive point spectrum of relative SU(2) BFSS}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. The relative $SU(2)$ BFSS operator is claimed to have infinitely many normalizable positive-energy eigenstates with eigenvalues tending to infinity.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
The gauge-invariant supercharge form first defines the relative operator. Selected $\operatorname{Spin}(9)$ symmetry sectors exclude the lowest transverse oscillator levels; the remaining oscillator energy confines those sectors, giving compact spectral pieces with normalizable positive-energy eigenstates despite escape channels in other sectors.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The relative $SU(2)$ BFSS operator is claimed to have infinitely many normalizable positive-energy eigenstates with eigenvalues tending to infinity. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

